\0
The Imperium's hover technology proved to be a considerable tactical advantage in most ground engagements. The ability of Imperium armor to move over water allowed them to dictate the circumstances of conflicts, and made it difficult for even the most capable Freedom Guard commanders to marshal decisive victories. The Freedom Guard felt they must obtain this technology in order to challenge the Imperium's dominion. The Freedom Guard discovered an Imperium research base on the planet Malik, where advances to the hover drive were being developed, and assaulted the base in an attempt to steal the vital technology.
\1
The security of the research site appears to have been compromised. A sizable Freedom Guard contingent has established a makeshift base, and an infiltrator has stolen vital information that may allow the Freedom Guard to duplicate our hover technology. Assault the Freedom Guard position and be sure to eliminate all traces of the enemy. We may be able to destroy the data before they can move it off world.
\n\n
\cOBJECTIVES\n
--> Protect the Hover Research Facility\n
--> Destroy the stolen technology by\n
\s\s\s\s eliminating all Freedom Guard forces
\2
The task before you is great, but you face it with courage.\n
\n
\cHISTORICAL OUTCOME:\n
A team of Freedom Guard infiltrators on Malik successfully stole plans for the Imperium's hover technology. A Freedom Guard armored column supporting the mission intercepted the Imperium as they attempted to hunt down the infiltrators. The Imperium contingent was destroyed, and Freedom Guard forces went on to level the research facility. Shortly after the engagement, Freedom Guard researchers were able to use the information to develop a hover tank of their own.
\3
Start again. Much rests on you.
